{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1552809271,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ3MzYyNjU4NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3233#issuecomment-473626584"},"message":"I am skeptical:\n\n### Technical issues:\n\n- the `description` argument *might* need the ability to get different values for different datasets\n- lumping together operations on multiple datasets is ugly from the Git history perspective already, and will remain ugly until https://github.com/datalad/datalad-revolution/pull/71 has a solution, which will allow for the introduction of proper commit message handling when working with dataset hierarchies (only tangentially related here)\n\n### Conceptual\n\n- which problem is being solved, other than \"it could be done\" -- nothing against that, but giving tons of stuff that is rather urgent, it would inform us about the priority of this issue\n\nOther than that I don't see an issue, but *please* let us have ONE `create` that needs to be adjusted first, not two.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1553033550,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ3NDYwNDk5MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3233#issuecomment-474604990"},"message":"\u003e * the `description` argument _might_ need the ability to get different values for different datasets\n\nif anything to differ, sure thing it would need multiple calls. I personally just resort to default description since I find it more useful than however I could potentially describe it for annex.\n\n\u003e * lumping together operations on multiple datasets is ugly from the Git history perspective already\n\nI would disagree. One of the DataLad's goals is to blur the lines between datasets, i.e. often to  be able to use them as we use directories. And we do make commits affecting multiple directories.\nI might want to create a collection of subdatasets preparing for multi subject/session study, so I ideally would like to do `datalad create -m \"Creating datasets for my 10 initial subjects\" sub-00{1..10}`.  I might want to create a default layout `datalad create code data images` to keep each component separately.  I really do not see why not to allow it if it could be easily done.\n\n\n\n\u003e * which problem is being solved, other than \"it could be done\" -- nothing against that, but giving tons of stuff that is rather urgent, it would inform us about the priority of this issue\n\n+1 on that\n\n\n\n\u003e _please_ let us have ONE `create` that needs to be adjusted first, not two.\n\n+10 on that ;-)","files":null},{"type":2,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1558334600,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE3OlJlbmFtZWRUaXRsZUV2ZW50MjM1MjA4NjQ1OQ=="},"title":"Make create take multiple PATHs arguments","was":"Make create take multiple PATHs arguments"}]}